---
/**
 * /terms — first-pass Terms of Service.
 *
 * A working draft written in the site's plain-language register for
 * counsel to review, replacing the "being prepared" placeholder. The
 * protective positions a young analytics company needs are all here:
 * results are decision-support estimates, the service ships as is
 * during beta, liability is capped at fees paid, customers own their
 * content and indemnify for it, and the model, software and marks stay
 * Lumecon's. Nothing on this page claims acceptance from anyone; the
 * signup flow will collect acceptance once counsel finalizes the text.
 */
import { site } from '../config';
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Lumecon"
  description="Terms of Service for the Lumecon platform and the Cedar product family: Cedar Impact, Cedar Commons, Cedar Grove and Cedar, the AI economic analyst. Covers software, subscriptions and advisory."
  canonical="https://lumecon.ai/terms"
  keywords="Lumecon terms of service, economic impact analysis terms, Cedar AI terms, Lumecon legal"
>
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <div class="date">
    Working draft, under review by counsel. These terms take effect when you are asked to accept
    them, not before.
  </div>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">1. Who we are and what these terms cover</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Lumecon is an economic analysis platform operated by {site.legalEntity}. These terms govern
        the Lumecon software, websites, subscriptions and advisory services, including the Cedar
        product family (Cedar Impact, Cedar Commons, Cedar Grove and Cedar&trade;, the AI
        economic analyst) across lumecon.ai. By creating an account or using the service you
        agree to these terms on behalf of yourself and, where applicable, the organization you
        represent.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">2. The service, including beta access</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Lumecon is offered in phases. During any beta or early-access period, features may change,
        pause or end without notice, and access may be granted, limited or withdrawn at our
        discretion. Beta access is provided so you can evaluate the platform; it creates no
        entitlement to any particular feature, output, uptime or continued access.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">3. Accounts</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        You are responsible for your account credentials and for activity under your account.
        Accounts belong to the organization that pays for them and may be reassigned within that
        organization. You must be at least 18 and authorized to act for the organization you
        register. We may suspend accounts that violate these terms or put the service or other
        customers at risk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">4. Subscriptions and fees</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Paid plans are annual, priced as published or as agreed in an order form, and payable in
        advance. Subscriptions renew for successive annual terms unless either party gives notice
        before renewal. Fees are exclusive of taxes; you are responsible for applicable taxes other
        than taxes on our income. Except where the law requires otherwise, fees are not refundable.
        Plan prices may change at renewal with advance notice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">5. Your content</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        You keep ownership of the documents, data and other material you bring to the service. You
        grant {site.legalEntity} the license needed to host, process and display that material in order
        to operate, secure and support the service for you. You are responsible for having the rights
        to the material you upload and for its accuracy. We may use aggregated and de-identified information
        derived from use of the service to improve the platform, in ways that do not identify you or your
        organization.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">6. Results are estimates</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Lumecon results are decision-support estimates. They describe likely economic relationships
        given the data and assumptions stated in each analysis, and they are labeled as estimates
        everywhere they appear. They are not financial, legal, tax or investment advice, they are
        not audits, and no result is a guarantee of any economic outcome. You are responsible for
        the decisions you make with them and for confirming the assumptions each analysis states.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">7. Cedar and AI outputs</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Cedar assists with intake, analysis, interpretation and reporting. Like all AI systems it
        can be wrong, and its suggestions are inputs to your judgment rather than substitutes for
        it. Assumptions Cedar proposes are surfaced for confirmation before results are finalized,
        and the person running an analysis is responsible for that confirmation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">8. Acceptable use</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        You agree not to misuse the service. That includes attempting to breach its security,
        probing or overloading it, reselling or sublicensing access without an agreement that allows
        it, scraping the service, using it to build a competing product, removing proprietary
        notices, reverse engineering the software except where the law permits, or presenting
        Lumecon outputs in a way that misstates what they are or how they were produced.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">9. Intellectual property</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        The Lumecon software, models, data architecture, documentation and websites are the
        exclusive property of {site.legalEntity} and are protected by intellectual property law; Lumecon&rsquo;s
        technology is patent pending. Lumecon, We luminate economies, Cedar, Local Economic Impact, Tribal
        Economic Impact and Global Economic Impact are trademarks of {site.legalEntity}. These terms
        grant you a right to use the service, not any ownership in it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">10. Warranties and disclaimers</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        The service is provided as is and as available. To the fullest extent the law allows, {
          site.legalEntity
        } disclaims all warranties, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular
        purpose and non-infringement, and does not warrant that the service will be uninterrupted, error-free
        or that any output will be accurate or complete.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">11. Limitation of liability</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        To the fullest extent the law allows, {site.legalEntity} will not be liable for indirect, incidental,
        special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data or goodwill, however
        arising. Our total liability for all claims arising out of or relating to the service is limited
        to the fees you paid for the service in the twelve months before the event giving rise to the
        claim, or one hundred dollars if you have paid no fees.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">12. Indemnification</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        You will defend and indemnify {site.legalEntity} against claims arising from the material you
        bring to the service, your use of results in violation of these terms, or your violation of law
        or the rights of a third party.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">13. Termination</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        You may stop using the service at any time. We may suspend or terminate access for material
        breach of these terms that is not cured after notice, or immediately where the breach puts
        the service or others at risk. On termination your right to use the service ends; sections
        that by their nature should survive (including ownership, disclaimers, liability limits and
        indemnification) survive.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">14. Changes and governing law</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the service evolves; material changes will be notified and
        apply going forward from their effective date. The governing law and venue for these terms
        will be stated here when counsel finalizes them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Counsel:</strong>{' '}{site.counsel}<br />Contact: <a
      href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
      class="note-link">{site.email}</a
    >
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
